      "summaryMarkdown": "This is a full review at the repaired snapshot. The first review's verdict was failed and left no stored review to reattest.\n\n**What holds:**\n- **`RunMetrics` reaches every layer.** It flows through `TextRun`, `FontRun` (unresolved, which is acceptable: the derived `Hash`/`Eq` put it in all four cache keys and the scratch pool is untouched), the merge loops and `shapes_as`.\n- **The shapers report per-run sizes.** CoreText maps by string index and cosmic sizes through `Attrs::metrics`. The web fallback now keeps the metrics.\n- **One shared spacing/shift post-pass.** It splits shaped runs on a shift change and leaves lines without metrics unchanged.\n- **Paint uses each run's size.** Strikethroughs come from the run's size and shift only.\n- **Proof:** the focused groups and lane checks, plus the RayX `..Default::default()` pairing.\n\nAll five earlier findings are resolved.",
